    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and favorable platoon splits against struggling arms. **Jose Caballero** (80.26) stands out as our premier play; his matchup against Abbott provides a massive 18% skill boost and a rare dynamic platoon edge that catapults him into our elite tier. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (79.53) remains a foundational start. Despite facing a mid-tier arm in Bradley, his ability to capitalize on the opposing pitcher's slow delivery\u2014combined with the high-leverage #3 lineup spot\u2014makes him our most potent weapon for closing the gap in the scarcest category. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.58) also project as strong starts, both benefiting from soft matchups against Ure\u00f1a and Corbin, respectively, where park factors and order placement provide clear efficiency floors.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Cole Young**, who landed just shy of the starting threshold with a 38.08 score. While he presents long-term value, the combination of a tough outing against Early and our strict \"Below 40\" bench policy kept him out of the mix, as we prioritize efficiency to manage our limited game caps. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the IL statuses of **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, whose absences force our depth to carry the load. We are particularly cautious regarding **Dalton Rushing** (43.96) and **Zach McKinstry** (42.06); both occupy the bottom of the order and face significant platoon disadvantages against Rogers and Newcomb, keeping them at the very edge of our starting viability. Owners should monitor the weather for any late-breaking system alerts that could dampen these matchups, though for now, the data confirms a focused attack against the weaker rotations of the day.",
